        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Design Principles\n\n## Events represent change\n\nAn event should describe something that happened, is happening, or is expected to happen. It should not merely be a timestamp attached to another node.\n\n## Keep the event node restrained\n\nThe canonical node identifies and summarizes the event. Participants, causes, outcomes, phases, evidence, and related works belong in the graph.\n\n## Support both moments and durations\n\nThe same template should represent a brief announcement, a conference lasting several days, or a war unfolding across years.\n\n## Reuse shared vocabulary\n\nPeople, Organizations, Events, and future Place templates should share roles, relationships, claims, evidence, sources, media, and works.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1784479326280,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
