      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# New Class: `participation`\n\nParticipation connects a person or organization to an event while preserving role, status, time, and evidence.\n\n## Shape\n\n`Person → Participation → Event`\n\nor\n\n`Organization → Participation → Event`\n\n## Suggested fields\n\n- Participation kind\n- Optional role reference\n- Event-specific capacity\n- Start time\n- End time\n- Attendance status\n- Assertion status: confirmed, reported, alleged, disputed, or unknown\n- Notes\n\n## Example kinds\n\n- Organizer\n- Host\n- Speaker\n- Attendee\n- Performer\n- Competitor\n- Witness\n- Victim\n- Responder\n- Sponsor\n- Opponent\n- Signatory\n\nThis class prevents important event roles from collapsing into anonymous edges.\n\nProvenance belongs in connected Claim → Evidence → Source nodes.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1784479326280,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
