        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# New Class: `event-phase`\n\nRepresents a meaningful internal stage or subevent.\n\n## Suggested fields\n\n- Name\n- Phase kind\n- Sequence\n- Start time\n- End time\n- Summary\n- Status\n- Parent event\n\n## Examples\n\n- Conference session\n- Trial hearing\n- Campaign period\n- Battle\n- Investigation stage\n- Product-launch keynote\n- Voting period\n- Emergency response phase\n\nA phase should be used when the event has internal structure worth navigating. Minor chronological details can remain ordinary timeline entries or notes.\n\n## Boundary\n\nA phase belongs to one parent event. A separately meaningful occurrence should remain a full Event connected by a relationship rather than being demoted to a phase.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1784479326280,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
