          }
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# New Class: `outcome`\n\nRepresents a result attributed to an event.\n\n## Suggested fields\n\n- Name\n- Outcome kind\n- Summary\n- Effective date\n- Subject reference\n- Status\n- Confidence\n- Intended or unintended\n- Time horizon: immediate, intermediate, or long-term\n\n## Examples\n\n- Decision\n- Election result\n- Policy change\n- Product release\n- Casualty report\n- Agreement\n- Acquisition completion\n- Cancellation\n- Organizational change\n\nOutcomes should remain distinguishable from claims. A claim may assert that an outcome occurred, while evidence and sources support or challenge that assertion.\n\nProvenance belongs in connected Claim → Evidence → Source nodes. The Outcome models a result; a Claim records whether it occurred or whether the event caused it.",
