      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Causes and Context\n\nEvents rarely float alone. They emerge from prior conditions and often trigger later events.\n\nUseful relationships include:\n\n- Caused by → Event, Decision, Condition, Person, or Organization\n- Triggered by → Event\n- Response to → Event or Claim\n- Part of → Event\n- Preceded by → Event\n- Followed by → Event\n- Concurrent with → Event\n- Changed → Person, Organization, Place, Policy, or Work\n\nCausation should be handled carefully. Where responsibility or cause is disputed, represent it as a sourced `claim` rather than presenting the edge as settled fact.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1784479326280,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
