          "position": {
            "side": "right",
            "offset": 0.5
          }
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Reuse Existing Classes\n\nThe Event Template should reuse the shared research vocabulary:\n\n- `role`\n- `relationship`\n- `life-event`\n- `work`\n- `media`\n- `claim`\n- `evidence`\n- `source`\n- `quote`\n\nExamples:\n\n- A speech or report may be a `work`.\n- Photos and recordings are `media`.\n- Statements made during the event may be `quote` nodes.\n- Disputed participant counts remain `claim` nodes.\n- Documents, recordings, and reporting become `source` and `evidence` nodes.\n\n`life-event` may remain useful when an event specifically marks a person's biography, while the canonical `event` class represents the shared occurrence itself.\n\n## Compatibility rule\n\nThe canonical `event` represents the shared occurrence. A `life-event` represents that occurrence’s biographical significance to one person and should not duplicate the full event.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "create",
          "updatedAt": 1784479326280,
          "reason": "node-batch-create"
        }
      }
    },
