      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Suggested Codex Implementation Plan\n\n1. Duplicate the structural skeleton of the Person or Organization Template.\n2. Rename declaration identity and surfaces for Event.\n3. Add the canonical `event` node.\n4. Preserve bridges for reusable research classes.\n5. Create node-class graphs for:\n   - `event`\n   - `participation`\n   - `event-phase`\n   - `outcome`\n6. Create Overview, Research, and Icon surfaces.\n7. Add lightweight examples demonstrating:\n   - one person participant\n   - one organization participant\n   - one event phase\n   - one outcome\n   - one related work or media item\n   - one sourced claim\n8. Validate all bridge refs, class bindings, surface IDs, node IDs, and declaration dependencies.\n9. Instantiate at least three substantially different event graphs before stabilizing the schema.\n\n## Proposed location\n\n`github://mikemartinez1974/public/events/template/event-template.node`\n\nThe first version should prioritize compatibility with People and Organizations over exhaustive event taxonomy.",
        "memo": "",
        "link": "",
        "visibilityRole": "browser",
